WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.234
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show,"

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:04.467
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:05.734
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:07.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
Well, this is nice.

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:10.701
Today, President Biden hosted
The White House's first-ever

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:13.934
Rosh Hashanah party to celebrate
the Jewish new year.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:17.701
Yeah. I think Biden was confused
because he ended his speech

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:20.567
by saying, "Now let's watch
Ryan Seacrest do the countdown."

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:22.667
And you go, "No."

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:24.200
Yeah, they celebrated today,

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.400
even though Rosh Hashanah
was Monday.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.801
That's like setting off
fireworks on the Ninth of July.

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:32.200
You know what I'm saying?
It's fun, but is it...

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.234
But it was a nice party,
although it got awkward when

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.834
Biden was
offered challah and said,

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:38.467
"You want me to speak louder?

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:41.067
I want that bread
you're holding.

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:43.534
Holla at your boy, Jack."

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.968
Then, a few hours later, the
president hosted a reception for

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:50.033
Hispanic Heritage Month.

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.634
Biden's staff was like,
"Hey, might as well

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.434
knock out all
the cringey gaffes in one day.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:55.400
You know what I'm saying?"

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.167
Biden held events
for the Jewish New Year

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.934
and Hispanic Heritage Month.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.067
Staffers watched Biden the way
Aaron Judge's mom

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.534
nervously watches his at bats.

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:04.000
Like, "Come on, buddy.
You can do this.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.901
You can do this. Don't mess..."

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:07.834
Well, get this --
in a televised address,

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.400
Vladimir Putin admitted
that Russia made mistakes

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.734
in how they drafted troops
for the war.

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:14.834
And then Putin broke into
the most depressing version of

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:15.934
"My Way" you've ever heard.

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:17.167
He's like...

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.067
[ Russian accent ]
♪ Regrets, I have a few ♪

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:22.834
♪ But, then again,
too few to mention ♪

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.200
[ Normal voice ] Meanwhile
today, Putin illegally claimed

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.601
four regions of Ukraine
as part of Russia.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:30.734
And to celebrate,
Putin and a few other leaders

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:31.901
had a pretty
interesting handshake.

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:32.968
Take a look at this.

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:39.701
[ Applause ]

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:41.467
-Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:47.234
-What?
-Oh!

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:48.334
-Rest easy, Russia.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:51.234
That guy's
coordinating your war.

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:52.767
That handshake looked like
a sandwich

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:54.567
made up of tiny white sausages,
didn't it?

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:57.067
-Ew!
-Well, this is big.

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.734
Earlier tonight,
Elon Musk hosted

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:00.767
Tesla's
Artificial Intelligence Day,

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:03.400
and he was expected to
unveil Tesla Bot,

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.234
a humanoid robot
designed to help with

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:06.801
boring, repetitive tasks,

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:08.934
stuff that humans
don't want to do anymore.

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:10.467
For example, Tesla Bot can...

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:13.567
or it can...

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.601
It can...

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:20.901
Then it can...

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:13.300
-Wow!

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:16.467
-Some movie news.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.400
Today, 29 years after
the original,

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.667
"Hocus Pocus 2"
premiered on Disney+.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.033
The movie looks great.

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:26.701
It's about three witches
who come back to life

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:29.434
after Lizzo starts playing
a 200-year-old flute.

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:31.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.534
Hey, did you guys see this?

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:38.400
Tomorrow is former president
Jimmy Carter's 98th birthday.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.100
-Ooh!
-Yeah, and this is exciting.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.734
He's also going to run
for a second term.

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:44.300
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.100
It's always nice to
hear about a famous Jimmy

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.400
who doesn't host a
late-night talk show, isn't it?

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.667
And, finally, I read that a
group of paleontologists

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:54.968
just found fish teeth
that are 14 million years older

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.934
than any teeth
found from any other species.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:04:00.267
We actually got in contact with
the paleontologists

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:01.667
responsible for the find.

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.334
Here's what they had to say.
The first one said...

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:07.000
This next one said...

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:14.968
And, finally,
the last scientist said...

